		"name": "linked-me_api",
		"description": "linked-me REST API\n\n## Response format\n\nAll success responses include a machine-readable `code` field for client-side i18n:\n```json\n{ \"message\": \"Logged out successfully\", \"code\": \"auth.logout.success\" }\n```\n\nAll error responses are normalized to:\n```json\n{\n  \"statusCode\": 401,\n  \"error\": \"Unauthorized\",\n  \"message\": \"Invalid credentials\",\n  \"code\": \"auth.login.invalid_credentials\"\n}\n```\n\nThe `code` field follows the format `module.action.result`. It is always present on business errors and success messages. It may be absent on framework-level errors (e.g. validation 400).\n\nAll available codes are defined in `src/common/constants/response-codes.ts`.\n\nAuthentication uses HttpOnly cookies: call auth/login once, Postman's cookie jar sends the cookies on every following request. Over http://localhost, set COOKIE_SECURE=false in the API .env.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "2920763"
	},
